A||||5||Tom88gt||removing lower 88 ball joint?||||5||
Z||000000||Tom88gt||11-17-2000||08:56 PM||||Does anyone know how to remove the lower ball joint on an '88 without removing the control arm from the car?  I don't have the special GM tool that is shown on page 270 of the Haynes manual.  I got a loaner tool from Autozone.  Their ball joint separator does not fit well and may even damage the control arm.  I've heard of possible spot welds but I can't find any.  If I go to a GM dealer and buy this special tool, how much is it and would anyone want to buy it (at a discount) from me once I'm finnished?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||11-17-2000||09:14 PM||||I changed my sons on his 88GT but I borrowed a ball joint tool- looks like a giant "C" clamp. Did it without removing the A arm. A ball joint separator is not the same tool as a ball joint press. Pep Boys didn't have the right tool either. BTW no welds on the '88||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tom88gt||11-17-2000||09:19 PM||||The Autozone tool was a C-clamp thing too.  But the part that holds the control arm does not fit at all.  It does not allow the bottom of the ball joint to drop out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||11-17-2000||10:07 PM||||To remove- I blocked the A arm and drove the ball joint out with a BFH. Just used the press with some big sockets that I had for installation. Crude I know but it worked.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||11-17-2000||11:01 PM||||I also use the big hammer method.  A 10 pound sledge does wonders!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phoenix||11-18-2000||08:40 PM||||When I did mine last summer I used a press.  Once you have the lower joint seperated from the knuckle taking the lower a-arm off is a snap. 2 bolts and it off.  I have a small 8 ton press and it took all it had to press 'em out.  New ones went in smoothly.||||reg||1
